  "text": "Dubai registered 11,041 residential sales totaling AED 32,077,251,613 in the last four weeks, a 9.2% increase in volume and 16.5% rise in value compared to the previous period. Mortgage registrations reached 4,312, recorded separately from sales. The median residential price per square foot stood at AED 1,672, down 1.3% from the prior four-week median of AED 1,694. Off-plan transactions accounted for 58.7% of sales, a decrease from 64.7% in the previous window.\n\nRental activity showed 93,471 Ejari contracts with a renewal share of 50.3%. The median annual residential rent was AED 70,000. Top performing areas by sales volume over twelve weeks include Dubai South with 3,842 sales and Jumeirah Village Circle with 2,259. Down Town Jabal Ali recorded 1,939 sales. Estimated gross yields for these areas range from 4.7% in Dubai South to 6.3% in Jumeirah Village Circle.\n\nPrice momentum varies significantly by location. Al Yufrah 1 saw a 42.2% increase in median price per square foot over twelve weeks, while Dubai Industrial City rose 12.2%. Conversely, Palm Jumeirah cooled with an 18.4% decline, followed by Palm Deira at 13.2% and Al Hebiah First at 11.1%. Highest estimated gross yields were found in Zaabeel First at 9.1% and International City Phase 1 at 8.6%, both for flats.\n\nInvestors should note that 1,015 sales in the last 60 days deviated more than 35% from comparable medians. These figures are derived from registered DLD data and Ejari contracts. Medians and benchmarks exclude bulk deals, partial shares, portfolio blocks, mortgages, gifts, and statistical outliers.",
